this weekend 200 europeans took part in  a historic event bringing together  citizens from 27 member states  people from all walks of life came to  the european parliament in strasbourg to  participate in the first european  citizens panel of the conference on the  future of europe  we wanted to start to hear your desires  your demands your ideas your intentions  your fears also your hopes  about uh the future of europe for three  days they discussed issues including  tackling youth unemployment better  social protection for all workers and  the importance of access to sports and  culture for everyone i think it's uh  an opportunity of a lifetime meeting so  many people from so much countries  everyone brings their own story brings  their own piece to the puzzle and it's  just so amazing colorful both in small  working groups and all together they  debated how to make the eu more  sustainable and socially just citizens  highlighted the challenges and  opportunities of digitalization and ai  especially  another 200 eu citizens will participate  in next weekend's panel on european  values and democracy this will be the  second of four panels covering key  themes related to the future of europe  the outcome of the panels will help  shape the conference conclusions in 2022  [Music]
 

